# recursive-shared-mutex

[AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) is the rule set. Cursor needs an always-on `.mdc`
entry point, so the rules a change can break silently are repeated here; the
reasoning is in AGENTS.md.

- C/C++ sources: **UTF-8 with BOM + CRLF**. `clang-format` writes CRLF but never
  a BOM. Repair with `python3 scripts/check_repo_rules.py --fix`.
- **120 columns**, tab-indented; `.clang-format` is the authority.
- Windows libraries through `target_link_libraries`, never `#pragma comment(lib)`.
- Headers: `#pragma once` first, no `using namespace` at namespace scope.
- `project(VERSION)` == `RSM_VERSION_MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH`; `CHANGELOG.md` keeps an
  `## [Unreleased]` section.
- The underlying `std::shared_mutex` must never be re-entered by the same thread
  (`[thread.sharedmutex]`); `try_*` members must not throw on the acquire path.
- Nothing may hold a pointer into the per-thread slot table across operations or
  across threads.
